sbi_lens: reach the tensorflow_probability JAX substrate by import, not by attribute.

Target:  sbi_lens @ d239796b30027ccb12b289e4c14fd61fbdec4d61 (the commit this project pins)
Apply:   patch -p1 from the sbi_lens *package* root, i.e. the directory containing normflow/

    patch -p1 -d "$(python -c 'import sbi_lens, os; print(os.path.dirname(sbi_lens.__file__))')" \
          < patches/sbi_lens_tfp.patch

WHY
Six modules of that commit reach the JAX substrate through an attribute of the top-level
package:

    import tensorflow_probability as tfp
    tfp = tfp.substrates.jax                 # bijectors.py, simulator/utils.py, gen_dataset/*
    tfp = tfp.experimental.substrates.jax    # normflow/models.py, normflow/train_model.py

Neither attribute is there on tensorflow-probability 0.25.0, the version this project pins.
`tfp.experimental.substrates` was removed in tfp >= 0.20. `tfp.substrates` is a lazily
loaded submodule: it only becomes an attribute of `tensorflow_probability` once something
has already imported it. So in a clean interpreter

    python -c "import sbi_lens.normflow.models"

dies with AttributeError on line 7 of normflow/bijectors/bijectors.py -- which models.py
imports on its own line 6, before its own substrate line is ever reached.

This patch rewrites all six lines to the supported, import-order-independent spelling

    from tensorflow_probability.substrates import jax as tfp

and keeps the upstream line as a comment directly above it, so the provenance stays visible.

BEHAVIOUR IS UNCHANGED
Both spellings bind the identical module object, `tensorflow_probability.substrates.jax`
(verified with `is` under tfp 0.25.0). Nothing else in these files is touched.

The patched normflow/models.py and normflow/train_model.py are byte-identical to the
sbi_lens copy in the environment the paper's numbers were produced in. The other four files
were left unpatched in that environment; they worked there only because this project's own
entry points import `tensorflow_probability.substrates.jax` before they touch sbi_lens.
Patching them removes that hidden import-order dependency without changing what any module
binds. (simulator/utils.py and gen_dataset/* additionally need lenstools / jax-cosmo / JaxPM,
which this project does not install -- they are patched for completeness, not because the
reproduction imports them.)

